    "body": "Hi @andytom! I'm not sure if there is a significant difference, but here's an interesting [wiki page I found in the scoop wikis](https://github.com/lukesampson/scoop/wiki/Chocolatey-Comparison).\r\n\r\nThey seem to stress on the fact that scoop isn't a _conventional_ package manager and it also alleviates the need to have _raised admin rights_ during installation. While that may be the case, I don't still see why chocolatey would be in any case less ideal.\r\n\r\nFor comparison sake, Chocolatey has more packages (4000+) and much larger user base. Here's a [summary of this comparison on slant](https://www.slant.co/versus/6470/6471/~chocolatey_vs_scoop).\r\n\r\n(We could alternatively mention both the installation options in the docs, and leave it up to the user to decide)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
